## 15. Release stages and test pyramid

1. **RFC complete**: ownership, terminology, case matrix and compatibility approved. No engine status claim.
2. **Technical alpha**: pure deterministic SRGBL package, synthetic fixtures, adversarial test, isolated versioning. No reviewed outputs claim.
3. **Research beta**: reproducible derived build, same result on API/static/browser, annotation review workflow, rights coverage, source correctness and per-tradition oversight.
4. **Public candidate**: five-level reader/trace, safe labels, citation, mobile accessibility, disputed state, no rank feature, agreement report and review decision.
5. **Stable method release**: source-locked docs/schema/rubric, CI, backward compat, migration, audit. Scientific validation may STILL be pending.

Minimum CI guardrails: corpus canonical hash unchanged unless intentionally scoped data update; `NO SYNTHETIC SCRIPTURE`, no unlicensed text, no cross-tradition rank, no invented miracles, no score-as-truth, no actor-frame jump, no confidence-inheritance, no duplicate canonical identities, and no unreviewed status promotion.

