## 17. Decisions to ratify at RFC review

- Explicit public MoonWitness brand and technical RGBL/TEXT distinction.
- SRGBL v8 local method namespace; external engine v7 not automatically upgraded.
- All derived score dimensions/version nomenclature; legacy 100 score review-only.
- Middle Point as categorical uncertainty first; no false neutral numeric calibration.
- Key Witness P18 `direction` formula change is a **new version**, not silent old-profile update.
- Islamic Quran-anchored mode vs neutral comparative mode and how readers choose/are informed of the lens.
- Who can mark `reviewed`; P18 decisions 2,3,6 remain prerequisites.
- Whether all numeric scores stay research-only during pilot: **recommended YES**.
- Whether every public message requires human editorial review: **recommended YES**.
- How licensed/attributed theological claims and editorial/personal narratives are stored outside canonical text.

## 18. Definition of Done for the grandplan

Grandplan is ratified when the RFC and crosswalk identify all historical concepts with source/version/epistemic type; all new terms have unambiguous field types; key, witness, message, swing, correction, miracle claim, offside and treasure can coexist without collapsing epistemic boundaries; P18 and P19 dependencies are traceable; README and blueprint accurately describe *current* vs *planned* capabilities; an engineer can implement the first three P19 tasks without guessing; and no 'passed' label is applied to a task not actually tested and reviewed.

**Final declaration:** MoonWitness may help readers **unlock new, reviewable relationships**, not produce new scripture, new divine revelations, automatic miracle proof, or theological rankings. `SOURCE BEFORE CLAIM • WITNESS BEFORE MESSAGE • CONTEXT BEFORE CORRECTION • REVIEW BEFORE PUBLICATION`.
